        ": سَأَلَهُ رَجُلٌ وَ أَنَا حَاضِرٌ عَنْ مَالِ اَلْمَمْلُوكِ أَ عَلَيْهِ زَكَاةٌ فَقَالَ «لاَ وَ لَوْ كَانَ لَهُ أَلْفُ أَلْفِ دِرْهَمٍ وَ لَوِ اِحْتَاجَ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ مِنَ اَلزَّكَاةِ شَيْءٌ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1634 - Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated from Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) who said:\nA man asked him in my presence about the wealth of a slave: \"Is Zakat obligatory on it?\"\nThe Imam (as) replied: \"No, even if he possesses a million dirhams. Moreover, if he were in need, he would not be entitled to receive anything from Zakat.\""
        ]
      }
